# 0334 = 0333 + per-endpoint queue storage and FIFO allocation.
#   - Every endpoint slot gets its own GPD ring (TX 1 KB, RX 256 B
#     cached; slot 1 keeps the verified BSS/UC ring).
#   - Per-EP CSR/QMU/HIAR offsets follow the vendor mtu3 strides and
#     are only applied by the 0331 test-channel commands.
#   - ruby_epfifo_map() finally allocates FIFO segments the way vendor
#     ep_fifo_alloc() does: one 512 B unit class x (slot + 1) = 3 units
#     per endpoint on this IP, 16 units per direction, so EP1-5 fit
#     (0x0/0x600/0xc00/0x1200/0x1800) and EP6-8 are refused instead of
#     overlapping.
#   - T2 batch: t331 epmap | eptx ep [len] | eprx ep | epall [len].
#     epall brings up EP1-8 TX/RX once each in the same boot and then
#     restores the default EP1 pair.
# Default path is unchanged: everything is inert unless rubyep_test=1
# and a command runs; the boot log of the default image is identical to
# 0333 (no epfifo lines).
#
# Verified on the device (lite + default): 0331 lite matrix PASS
# (T0/T1/T3/T4), epmap 0x0/0x600/0xc00/0x1200/0x1800 + REJECT(units=3
# free=1) for EP6-8, epall ok_tx=3e tmo_tx=00 err_tx=1c0 ok_rx=3e
# err_rx=1c0 restore=0 with per-EP st=0, post-batch lite matrix PASS,
# default image WinUSB CM_PROB_NONE, no panic, fused=0.  Not covered:
# host-side data on EP2-8 (host tool still fixed on 0x81), RX slots only
# arm, concurrent multi-EP interference.
#
# patchset d87e666ff903ad8dc214773495feac827558ab53bf5b8fd3edfc30734c19ff71
# (305 files; 0001-0079 baseline + project patches through 0334)
